1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,070
[Step 1 · Originate]
The call originates at the End User, inside the customer's app.

2
00:00:02,070 --> 00:00:04,050
[Step 2 · Authenticate — Path 1: OAuth2]
ISV App requests an app-only OAuth2 token from Provider Entra ID (client_credentials) — a side call, no user involved.

3
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:07,794
[Step 3 · Cross the boundary — Private Link]
Traversing the Private Endpoint — Private Link, over Microsoft's backbone, NAT applied. No VNet peering involved.

4
00:00:07,794 --> 00:00:09,414
[Step 4 · Validate — Path 1: OAuth2]
Gateway validates the JWT (issuer, audience, claims) against Provider Entra ID.

5
00:00:09,414 --> 00:00:11,214
[Step 5 · Managed identity]
Gateway fetches its own managed-identity token for Foundry — a same-tenant hop, no cross-tenant AAD involved.

6
00:00:11,214 --> 00:00:13,194
[Step 6 · Forward]
Request forwarded to Microsoft Foundry over a same-tenant private endpoint.

7
00:00:13,194 --> 00:00:15,264
[Step 7 · Model call]
Foundry routes the request to Anthropic's Claude inference service.

8
00:00:15,264 --> 00:00:18,918
[Step 8 · Response]
Completion streams back: Anthropic to Foundry to Gateway.

9
00:00:18,918 --> 00:00:19,458
[Step 9 · Async metering]
Gateway emits token metrics to Azure Monitor — asynchronous, does not delay the reply.

10
00:00:19,458 --> 00:00:24,966
[Step 10 · Deliver]
Response crosses back over the same path to the ISV App and the End User.

11
00:00:24,966 --> 00:00:29,966
[Complete]
Flow complete — end to end, one round trip.
